{"name":"Willow Grey","hex":"#817b69","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"willow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous trees or shrubs in the genus Salix, in the willow family Salicaceae, found primarily on moist soils in cooler zones in the northern hemisphere.","The wood of these trees."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open and cleanse (cotton, flax, wool, etc.) by means of a willow.","To form a shape or move in a way similar to the long, slender branches of a willow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/willow"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Willow","blocks":[{"text":"Willows, also called sallows and osiers, of the genus Salix, comprise around 350 species of typically deciduous trees and shrubs. They are primarily found on moist soils in cold and temperate regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_si